# Backend architecture

- Read `docs/architecture/README.md` and `docs/architecture/conventions.md` before structural changes.
- Domain owns pure entities/enums/constants/policies. Application owns business services, DTOs, validators and ports. Infrastructure owns EF/SQL/security/email/storage adapters. Api owns HTTP and host composition.
- Domain cannot reference other project layers or EF/SQL/ASP.NET. Application references only Domain and framework-neutral libraries; never Infrastructure, EF/SQL, SMTP or ASP.NET.
- Business services belong in `Application/Services/{Auth,Admin,Portal,Backoffice}`. Infrastructure/Services contains only technical services. Do not replace business logic with pass-through Application wrappers.
- Define specific repository methods in Application and implement them in Infrastructure/Repositories. Return materialized data, never DbContext, DbSet, IQueryable or provider exceptions.
- Controllers inject Application service interfaces, never concrete Infrastructure services/repositories/DbContext/workers. Host composition may call Infrastructure DI/startup entrypoints.
- Match namespaces to folders; use one file per controller. Keep DTO contracts explicit and typed while preserving existing HTTP JSON, routes and status codes.
- AddApplication registers use cases; AddInfrastructure registers adapters. Repositories, outbox and unit of work share a scoped DbContext.
- Preserve identity administration locks, permission/version checks, last-admin protection, serializable submissions and atomic conditional reviews. Translate EF/SQL errors at the adapter boundary.
- Queue email in the same unit of work; send SMTP outside retries. Keep avatar IO and atomic transfer-ticket storage behind Application ports.
- Do not change schema or overwrite scaffolded entities for a layer refactor. DbContext and mappings belong in Infrastructure/Data.
- Run the test csproj directly; the solution contains source projects only. LayerBoundaryTests must pass. SQL integration tests require TEKY_MIGRATION_TEST_CONNECTION and disposable databases.
- Use `-p:BaseOutputPath=bin/LayerVerification/` if a running API locks default DLLs. Report skipped tests and transient timeout reruns.
- Update architecture docs and role-mapping references with ownership/dependency changes.
